Setting the system up
---------------------
Make a directory, call it anything you want. Then assign SHOGUN: to that
one and put ALL files in this archive right into it...
Assigning SHOGUN: to DH1:ONLINE may look something like:

ASSIGN SHOGUN: DH1:ONLINE

That will do it.

Then edit the SHOGUN.CFG file. It's explained in the file what it's for.
(It's the game-log path and filename)

After that, make a directory within SHOGUN: thats called USERS.
To make that one, it may look something like:

MAKEDIR SHOGUN:USERS

Then it's up to your BBS-system how to set the whole thing up. The main
program of course is the 'SHOGUN' file. Just run it (you can even do so
from the CLI window!!!).


Shogun is a kind program that leaves the memory it has used after it and
as far as I know, there are no known buggs if something is set up
correctly.

Anyhow -> I take NO responsible for anything that may happen when you
          use this program. I havn't noticed anything that may crash your
          system and I hardly think you'll do either...


